{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017qsNYeTEuCvKDw9maGiLX8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents (`CLAUDE.md`, memory, and the locked North Stars), here is what Anchor **is**:\n\n## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A personal productivity / task-management system for J.C. Liechty**, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing. Tasks, projects, inbox, and domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) are all `.md` files you edit through a browser dashboard.\n\n- **It ships a self-contained local web app (`anchor_gui.py`)** â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that generates the dashboard HTML on every request, writes changes back to the markdown files, and runs persistently in the background as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777`.\n\n- **It ships a CLI mirror (`anchor.py`)** with the same logic â€” done/cancel/save/restore/add/capture commands plus a static `dashboard.html` generator â€” so every operation is available without the GUI.\n\n- **Tasks move through a real lifecycle** (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored), each with optional notes, archived to reviewable files (`CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`).\n\n- **It ships a daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`)** that runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and state transition (all model calls stubbed, never live), and writes a dated report; failures surface as a red banner on the dashboard.\n\n- **Its largest subsystem is the \"R&D Control Surface\" â€” a built-in mission-control / cockpit for AI \"trio\" work** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill pipeline). This has been built and merged across four iterations:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated summaries, \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, deliverable pinning, an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real **ConPTY terminals** (the one declared native-dependency exception, `pywinpty`), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a stacking window manager, proactive cached project summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (guarded to never bind port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (merged 2026-06-13, commit `38fd70e`, 637 tests passing) â€” each lane is a **tile with one honest status light** (green/amber/red/grey) that **expands an inline panel in place** showing a summary over a resizable terminal; a Claudeâ†”Gemini **engine toggle**, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch. It also fixed the repeating-prompt terminal bug by unwiring the old v2 REPL from the cockpit.\n\n- **Its core design rule is \"Python stdlib only, no external dependencies\"** â€” with exactly **one** declared, lazily-imported, optional exception (`pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem), enforced by an import scanner in `distro.py`. Everything stays accessible as plain text from any CLI tool.\n\nIn short: **Anchor is a single-folder, markdown-backed, locally-served personal task dashboard that has grown a sophisticated embedded cockpit for running and tracking AI-agent R&D sessions.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f77df875-57bd-4aad-9eaa-63f43d4754e5","uuid":"dfd44e3d-30b6-49ea-b148-aad742c03a19","request_id":"req_011Cc1JF62CiXc1za8bXouUF"}
